            <ArticleTitle>[Differential selection of anti-anginal drugs in stable stenocardia in relation to the data of central and intracardiac hemodynamics].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>44-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Rheography and echocardiography were used to study central and intracardiac hemodynamic parameters in 196 patients with Functional Classes I-II from the screening of the main antianginal drugs during an acute pharmacological test under bicycle ergometric monitoring. It was established that the hemodynamic type of circulation and left ventricular end-diastolic and end-systolic volumes may be used as criteria for the differential choice of antianginal agents. The values of these parameters are given for sustac, propranolol, verapamil, nifedipine and sustac plus propranolol.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
